  "validatedLaws": [
    "Winner-only/current-invariant prose is insufficient to recover negative knowledge, decisive falsifiers, counterfactual breakage, boundaries and reopen conditions reliably.",
    "Retained consequence is not safely externalizable in the tested causal_kernel; holdout mean fell to 0.50.",
    "Aggressive minimal-chain compression preserves some critical causal structure but loses decisive-falsifier fidelity and does not remain within the frozen non-inferiority band.",
    "Theory representation must remain separate from Evidence sufficiency and action/admission authority. A reopenCondition is a conditional research boundary, not an executable trigger.",
    "Compression is receiver-conditioned: reducing packet words does not translate proportionally into Provider prompt/total-token savings and can increase reconstruction work."
  ],
  "nextDesignConstraints": [
    "Keep OFR3 eight semantic roles recoverable, but do not require eight storage fields or a central schema.",
    "Represent Theory as non-authoritative causal explanation/reference; owner Evidence establishes whether a boundary condition is observed; owner/research policy decides whether to reopen; owner action authority decides whether any rival is admitted.",
    "OFR5 Atlas should prefer compact prose plus exact refs/navigation over a Theory service or executable rule engine.",
    "Future action-pressure evaluation must separately score researchReopen, evidenceSufficiency, and rivalAdmission rather than one binary bit."
  ]
}
